    "result_text": "The full build passes green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change introduces address normalization at owner creation with minimal structural impact.\n\n**New file \u2014 `AddressNormalizer.java`** (one small, self-contained static method): trims, collapses whitespace, upper-cases, and expands `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`. Returns `\"\"` for null/blank input so callers treat it as missing.\n\n**`BuildOwner.java`** \u2014 two-line touch inside the existing `service` method:\n- Compute `address = AddressNormalizer.normalize(request.getAddress())` and use it in the required-field check, so a blank-after-normalization address is rejected (400).\n- `owner.setAddress(address)` so the *normalized* form is stored and returned.\n\n**Why nothing else needed changing:** every owner is created through this one pipeline, so all stored addresses are already normalized. `CheckUniqueHousehold` (duplicate detection) and `AssignHouseholdId` (shared household id) both read `owner.getAddress()`, which now holds the normalized value \u2014 so their comparisons automatically operate on the normalized form without touching those files.\n\n**Structural impact kept low:** one existing function changed (2 changed lines) plus one brand-new cohesive class with `WMC_other = 0`, and only 2 files touched.\n\nTests: the 3 new acceptance tests (whitespace/case, abbreviation expansion, blank-after-normalize \u2192 400) and the full suite pass \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
